  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read spec FR-17 + design (§6.2/§6.5/§8), ADR-046 (task 007), ADR-045, the `docs-architecture` skill, and the existing `communication-intelligence-architecture.md` + `communication-service-architecture.md` to find the right insertion points.</step>
    <step order="2">Verify against code: read the shipped 040 resolver, 021/030/031 ingestor + capture pipeline, 004/005 schema, 010/011 ACS integration — ground each section in real code entry points.</step>
    <step order="3">Extend the canonical doc with: thread data model (entity + lookup + child table + topologies + privacy/point-forward), `IThreadResolver` (direction-symmetric; email vs chat threading; the email-grouping feature), ACS transport (transport-vs-record, identity/token, retention, membership projection, no client SDK), and the inbound ingestor seam (Event Grid pipeline + idempotency/echo-dedup).</step>
    <step order="4">Cross-reference ADR-046 + related ADRs; cross-link the data-model doc for the schema detail. Use code entry-point pointers, not code dumps.</step>
